# The Actions grid's Message, Set Mount and Clear Track, in the cells the .resx gives them.
#
# Message (2,4) asks "Enter Message to be logged" and sends it as a STATUSTEXT of severity 5, which
# the vehicle writes to its log; Cancel sends nothing. Set Mount (1,3) sends the mode chosen in
# CMB_mountmode (0,3) - the documented values of the first of MNT1_DEFLT_MODE, MNT_DEFLT_MODE and
# MNT_MODE, starting on the first - as MNT_MODE where the vehicle has that parameter and as
# DO_MOUNT_CONTROL's seventh parameter where it does not, as SITL does not; both are waited for.
# Clear Track (4,3) takes the route flown off the map, which records it again from the next
# position. Raw Sensor View (3,2) is a window of its own and is drawn dimmed.
# `GCSViews/FlightData.cs:1101-1107, 1255-1271, 1392-1415, 2718-2729, GCSViews/FlightData.Designer.cs:747-770`
#
# Needs SITL (a copter): tools/gui-test.sh tests/gui/fly-actionsgrid.gui -- tcp:127.0.0.1:5760

screen fly
window 1600x1200
budget 9

# The vehicle first: a click before its first heartbeat is a click the screen may forget
# (vehicle.connected only says the link is open).
expect vehicle.count > 0
click fly-tab-actions
expect fly.tab tabActions
expect fly.page.overflow 0

click fly-sendmsg
expect fly.prompt Enter Message to be logged
type hello log
expect fly.prompt.value hello log
click fly-prompt-ok
expect fly.prompt none
expect fly.sent STATUSTEXT severity=5 text=hello log

click fly-sendmsg
type not sent
click fly-prompt-cancel
expect fly.prompt none
expect fly.sent STATUSTEXT severity=5 text=hello log

# The list starts on its first mode.
expect fly.mountmode ~ 0 Retract
click fly-mountmode
expect fly.sent COMMAND_LONG MAV_CMD_DO_MOUNT_CONTROL 0,0,0,0,0,0,0
expect fly.ack ~ MAV_CMD_DO_MOUNT_CONTROL:

click fly-mountmode-list
click fly-mountmode-2
expect fly.mountmode ~ 2 M
click fly-mountmode
expect fly.sent COMMAND_LONG MAV_CMD_DO_MOUNT_CONTROL 0,0,0,0,0,0,2
expect fly.page.overflow 0

# Clear Track takes the route recorded so far - one point while SITL stands still - and the next
# position starts it again.
expect fly.track.cleared none
expect fly.track > 0
click fly-cleartrack
expect fly.track.cleared > 0
expect fly.track > 0
